# Wrangler local secrets stub (loaded by `wrangler dev`).
#
# Real secrets for production are managed via `wrangler secret put`.
# Do NOT commit a real .dev.vars file.
#
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and replace placeholders before running
# `wrangler dev`. 0.1.0 Foundation has no bindings that require
# secrets; this stub exists so the .gitignore whitelist (`!.dev.vars.example`)
# is satisfied.

# Example placeholder (none used by 0.1.0 Foundation release):
# SOME_BINDING_TOKEN="replace-me"

# 0.3.0 Foundation: Better Auth secret. Generate a 32+ byte random string
# locally; production is provisioned via `wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`.
# Required by Better Auth's session signing. See ADR-0009.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-32-byte-random-string"

# 0.3.0 Foundation: Better Auth base URL (origin of the deployment).
# Local development: http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Production: https://<your-deployment>.workers.dev
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://127.0.0.1:3000"

# 0.3.0-extended: Home self-consumption API key (ADR-0011). Provision
# once per environment via `pnpm run bootstrap:home-api-key`. The
# plaintext is printed by that script and pasted here for local dev,
# or set as a Wrangler secret (`wrangler secret put
# MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY`) for remote. The home's reactions and
# access-counter server fns read this value to self-call
# `/api/v1/{reactions,access}/*` with the consumer scopes.
# MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY="mk_home_..."